{"id": "EUVD-2026-71307", "enisaUuid": "4611d127-3baf-38b8-9d41-28ad68f2d0d4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfuse: wait for FR_FINISHED on abort_on_kill to prevent use-after-free\n\nThe abort_on_kill path in request_wait_answer() calls fuse_abort_conn()\nand returns without waiting for FR_FINISHED.  If fuse_dev_do_write() is\nconcurrently processing the same request (FR_LOCKED set), the caller\nfrees req->args while it is still being accessed, causing a\nuse-after-free.\n\nFix this by jumping to the existing wait_event(FR_FINISHED) instead of\nreturning early.  The wait will not hang because fuse_abort_conn()\nensures all requests are ended.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:55:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:44:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a8bbb2a60513bf322170903c21462f0bf4f62be2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/715cb86e33cda43f5224cdc3fd5610c0b6a46f7a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64b0b5cacbd2fea88001464cb712c9dfc795b26e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3r92-fq36-p33j", "CVE-2026-80857"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0859dadf-c23b-3461-afec-8080775cefbd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "43bc2d49-eadc-39ad-a179-f9b6a4a9ce8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "4d4f1eae-1fc6-3cbf-8378-584308ef17cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.3"}, {"id": "7cb6a3b5-ca39-37b5-8096-0f67e6690d86", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0c7fca880a40a209a9c92be14143996d14b93ff6 <a8bbb2a60513bf322170903c21462f0bf4f62be2"}, {"id": "8db40202-a5f5-3857-9086-49e0692242a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.25 <6.18.50"}, {"id": "9c71308c-09b6-3e9b-acff-f25f8d2d399d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "b3e01035-d4e9-394e-8e94-3fd8824fe7f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ba6502a5-fda9-3491-a8d3-739730a03b57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "204aa22a686bfee48daca7db620c1e017615f2ff <715cb86e33cda43f5224cdc3fd5610c0b6a46f7a"}, {"id": "d3fe3543-d1be-3d20-b7bb-e3fdedc32816", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "204aa22a686bfee48daca7db620c1e017615f2ff <64b0b5cacbd2fea88001464cb712c9dfc795b26e"}, {"id": "dec1a728-17ea-39b4-a98f-0d2038f6f2c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0.2 <7.1"}, {"id": "f07d0f84-6e28-3ed7-82de-4c1916b2d632", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "300e812b882a174dca675d8028684001ad5826bc"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "795bb5cf-a231-3b1b-bf64-8dd4b55a3ac2", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}